    "result_text": "Done. The build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the one generator, now:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the owners already in that city, counted by filtering `ownerRepository.findAll()` on city (case-insensitive, trimmed), mirroring the existing `AssignNamesakeCount` pattern (there's no `countByCity` repository method). Example: `SYD-SMI-0007`.\n\n**`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 the membership number is the only value derived from the customerCode. It's built at runtime from `owner.getCustomerCode()` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it rebuilds on the new format automatically; I only refreshed its stale javadoc example (`SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). `membershipTier` in `OwnerMapper` derives from namesakeCount/email, not customerCode, so it's unaffected.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures.",
